# Android APK — fast build & install

Test phone ADB serial: `0015935A7000905`

## Default: one command (~20–40s)

```bash
npm run android:install
```

This runs `scripts/android-fast-install.sh`:
1. `vite build` (web only)
2. `rsync` dist → `android/app/src/main/assets/public` (skip slow/hung `cap sync` for JS-only)
3. `./gradlew assembleDebug` (incremental — keep daemon warm)
4. `adb install -r`

**Do not** use `clean`, `gradlew --stop`, or full `npm run android:build` for normal UI fixes.

## When to use the slow path

Only if native Android/Java/plugins/`capacitor.config` changed:

```bash
npm run android:build
adb -s 0015935A7000905 install -r android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
```

## Why installs felt slow before

- Vite/cap sync hung in sandbox or cold starts (minutes)
- `gradlew clean` / `--stop` killed the warm daemon
- Full Capacitor sync when only React/JS changed
- Package timeout after stopping daemons

## JDK

Project-scoped in `android/gradlew` → `/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@21/...`

## If Gradle breaks (dex / NoSuchFile)

```bash
cd android && ./gradlew --stop
rm -rf app/build build
./gradlew assembleDebug
```

Then go back to `npm run android:install` next time.
